{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MuCNZJ1QGEi1bqXLGoCEsB","type":"tool_result","content":"40\t\n41\tfunc (checker *nativeChecker) fsys() pose.Files { return pose.FilesOrNative(checker.files) }\n42\t\n43\tfunc (checker *nativeChecker) message(english, portuguese string) string {\n44\t\treturn cliText(checker.locale, english, portuguese)\n45\t}\n46\t\n47\t// issue emits one gate finding. The level used to be the literal string \"ERRO\"\n48\t// or \"AVISO\" printed as-is — a Portuguese anchor in an English interface, and a\n49\t// counter that compared prose to decide what had failed. The state comes from\n50\t// the closed vocabulary, its word is rendered in the reader's language, and the\n51\t// untranslated anchor a tool needs is the severity in `--json`\n52\t// (spec pose-cli-output-rendering-system R3, R8).\n53\tfunc (checker *nativeChecker) issue(state cliout.State, message string) {\n54\t\tchecker.renderer().Finding(cliout.Finding{State: state, Message: message})\n55\t\tif state == cliout.StateError {\n56\t\t\tchecker.errors++\n57\t\t} else {\n58\t\t\tchecker.warnings++\n59\t\t}\n60\t}\n61\t\n62\t// renderer resolves the checker's output lazily, so a caller that builds a\n63\t// checker for one sub-check — the tests do — still reports through the layer.\n64\tfunc (checker *nativeChecker) renderer() *cliout.Renderer {\n65\t\tif checker.out == nil {\n66\t\t\tchecker.out = render(checker.stdout, io.Discard)\n67\t\t}\n68\t\treturn checker.out\n69\t}\n70\t\n71\tfunc (checker *nativeChecker) failOrWarn(message string) {\n72\t\tif checker.mode == \"tolerant\" {\n73\t\t\tchecker.issue(cliout.StateWarning, message)\n74\t\t} else {\n75\t\t\tchecker.issue(cliout.StateError, message)\n76\t\t}\n77\t}\n78\t\n79\t// cmdCheck runs the strict/tolerant gate in the invoking shell's own locale\n80\t// (the command has no --locale flag of its own). cmdCheckWithLocale lets an\n81\t// internal caller that already resolved an explicit locale — `pose install`/\n82\t// `pose update`'s post-install gate, driven by their own --locale — report\n83\t// in that locale instead, matching the language the operator actually asked\n84\t// for on the outer command rather than whatever the shell's $LANG happens to\n85\t// be (spec pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes).\n86\tfunc cmdCheck(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n87\t\treturn cmdCheckWithLocale(root, args, stdout, stderr, cliLocaleValue())\n88\t}\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"2059d8bc-b7f1-40c2-b779-a2679df4dd5f","timestamp":"2026-11-11T00:20:33.141Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-239315660/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go","content":"\nfunc (checker *nativeChecker) fsys() pose.Files { return pose.FilesOrNative(checker.files) }\n\nfunc (checker *nativeChecker) message(english, portuguese string) string {\n\treturn cliText(checker.locale, english, portuguese)\n}\n\n// issue emits one gate finding. The level used to be the literal string \"ERRO\"\n// or \"AVISO\" printed as-is — a Portuguese anchor in an English interface, and a\n// counter that compared prose to decide what had failed. The state comes from\n// the closed vocabulary, its word is rendered in the reader's language, and the\n// untranslated anchor a tool needs is the severity in `--json`\n// (spec pose-cli-output-rendering-system R3, R8).\nfunc (checker *nativeChecker) issue(state cliout.State, message string) {\n\tchecker.renderer().Finding(cliout.Finding{State: state, Message: message})\n\tif state == cliout.StateError {\n\t\tchecker.errors++\n\t} else {\n\t\tchecker.warnings++\n\t}\n}\n\n// renderer resolves the checker's output lazily, so a caller that builds a\n// checker for one sub-check — the tests do — still reports through the layer.\nfunc (checker *nativeChecker) renderer() *cliout.Renderer {\n\tif checker.out == nil {\n\t\tchecker.out = render(checker.stdout, io.Discard)\n\t}\n\treturn checker.out\n}\n\nfunc (checker *nativeChecker) failOrWarn(message string) {\n\tif checker.mode == \"tolerant\" {\n\t\tchecker.issue(cliout.StateWarning, message)\n\t} else {\n\t\tchecker.issue(cliout.StateError, message)\n\t}\n}\n\n// cmdCheck runs the strict/tolerant gate in the invoking shell's own locale\n// (the command has no --locale flag of its own). cmdCheckWithLocale lets an\n// internal caller that already resolved an explicit locale — `pose install`/\n// `pose update`'s post-install gate, driven by their own --locale — report\n// in that locale instead, matching the language the operator actually asked\n// for on the outer command rather than whatever the shell's $LANG happens to\n// be (spec pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes).\nfunc cmdCheck(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n\treturn cmdCheckWithLocale(root, args, stdout, stderr, cliLocaleValue())\n}\n","numLines":50,"startLine":40,"totalLines":1373}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MuCNZJ1QGEi1bqXLGoCEsB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
